;;; gamma-function.scm -- THE IMPROPER INTEGRAL ON (0, +inf), THE GAMMA FUNCTION, ITS
;;; CONVERGENCE ON THE RIGHT HALF-PLANE, ITS HOLOMORPHY (PROPOSITION 3.59), GAMMA(1) = 1 AND
;;; GAMMA(z + 1) = z GAMMA(z), GAMMA(n + 1) = n!.
;;; (complex-analysis.pdf ch. 3, section 3.9: (96)-(101), Definition 3.58, Proposition 3.59.)
;;; Agent CA-6 of week 3 of the October roadmap (scratchpad/triage/WEEK3.md), 2026-10-04.
;;; Definitions: structure-library/gamma-function.scm (IMPROPER-INT-CONVERGES-TO, IMPROPER-INT,
;;; GAMMA-INTEGRAND, GAMMA-FUNCTION).  H below is the open right half-plane
;;; {w in CC : 0 < re w}, written literally (SEP gmu_ CC (< 0 (real-part gmu_))).
;;;
;;; CONTENTS (in proof order; every theorem bills modulo 0).
;;;  (1) right-half-plane-open, right-half-plane-in-slit          H is open; H lies in the slit plane
;;;  (2) real-interval-is-road, real-interval-trace               [a, b] with t |-> t, derivative 1, is a road
;;;  (3) cc-int-as-line-int, cc-int-in-cc-of-continuous,          CC-INT(f, a, b) of an f continuous on u
;;;      cc-int-split, cc-int-compare-primitive                     (with [a, b] in u) is that line integral;
;;;                                                                 additivity; |int f| <= re(G(b) - G(a))
;;;                                                                 when |f| <= re G' on [a, b]
;;;  (4) gamma-integrand-holomorphic                              w |-> w^{z-1} e^{-w} is holomorphic on H
;;;  (5) rr-positive-below-two, rr-above-two, improper-int-cauchy, the improper integral abstractly: the
;;;      improper-int-tail-bound, improper-int-unique,              Cauchy criterion (CC is complete), the
;;;      improper-int-value                                          tail bound, uniqueness, the value of IOTA
;;;  (6) cc-exp-magnitude, cc-exp-real-mono, cc-exp-log-real,      |e^v| = e^{re v}; exp and log on the line;
;;;      log-cc-exp-real, gamma-integrand-magnitude                 |t^{z-1} e^{-t}| = e^{(re z - 1) log t - t}
;;;  (7) log-nonneg-of-ge-one, gamma-integrand-bound-small,        estimate (96): t^{s0-1} on (0, 1] and
;;;      gamma-integrand-bound-large                                 e^{A(log 2A - 1) - t/2} on [1, +inf)
;;;  (8) ccint-in-right-half-plane, gamma-integrand-locint,        the two tails: |int_r1^r2| <= r2^{s0}/s0,
;;;      gamma-tail-small, gamma-tail-large                          |int_R1^R2| <= 2 e^{K - R1/2}
;;;  (9) log-monotone, rr-power-small-at-zero, rr-power-monotone,  the Cauchy condition of the double limit
;;;      exp-tail-small-at-infinity, exp-tail-monotone,
;;;      gamma-small-difference, gamma-large-difference
;;; (10) gamma-converges                                          THE CONVERGENCE (3): for 0 < re z the
;;;                                                               improper integral converges to GAMMA-FUNCTION(z)
;;; (11) cc-int-linear-combination, gamma-integrand-expansion,    the truncations are holomorphic (4): the
;;;      log-abs-bound-on-interval, gamma-integrand-bound-interval, quadratic estimate |e^v - 1 - v| <= |v|^2
;;;      gamma-integrand-quadratic, gamma-truncation-quadratic,    under the integral, then
;;;      gamma-truncation-holomorphic                                `cc-diff-on-local-quadratic'
;;; (12) gamma-truncation-error, gamma-holomorphic                THE THEOREM OF 3.9 (5): the truncations
;;;                                                               converge locally uniformly; holomorphic-uniform-limit
;;; (13) cc-int-of-derivative, gamma-at-one                       Gamma(1) = 1, equation (100)
;;; (14) gamma-product-derivative, rr-power-small-at-zero-plain,  Gamma(z + 1) = z Gamma(z), equation (101)
;;;      gamma-recursion
;;; (15) gamma-factorial                                          Gamma(n + 1) = n!, equation (102)
;;;
;;; THE ROUTES AND WHAT CHANGED FROM THE BRIEF'S ORDER.  None of the order; the routes:
;;; * Every integral over [r, R] is turned into the LINE integral along the real interval
;;;   road (2)-(3), so that continuity, existence of primitives, the modulus estimate, additivity,
;;;   linearity and the FUNDAMENTAL THEOREM (`line-int-of-derivative') come from the line-integral
;;;   laws for a function continuous on the half-plane.  The integrand is defined on H with CC-LOG
;;;   (the definitions file says why), so it is HOLOMORPHIC in w and `dk-holomorphic!' gives its
;;;   continuity in one call.  No real-variable calculus is done: every comparison integral is
;;;   evaluated by the fundamental theorem on an explicit holomorphic primitive
;;;   (`cc-int-compare-primitive': w^{s0}/s0 for the tail at 0, -2 e^{K - w/2} at infinity).
;;; * Convergence (3): the Cauchy condition of the double limit is reduced, by splitting at 1, to
;;;   one tail at 0 and one at infinity; `improper-int-cauchy' turns it into a limit through the
;;;   sequence g_k = int_{1/(k+1)}^{k+2} and `cc-complete'.  The notes' (96) bounds the tail at
;;;   infinity by M e^{-R}, which does not follow from e^{-t} t^{s-1} <= M (that bound is not
;;;   integrable); the proof uses (s - 1) log t <= A(log 2A - 1) + t/2 (from log y <= y - 1 at
;;;   y = t/2A), i.e. |integrand| <= C e^{-t/2}.
;;; * Holomorphy of the truncations (4), route (a) of the brief, without a difference quotient
;;;   and without a limit: T(x) - T(a) - (x - a) int e^{-t} t^{a-1} log t is the integral of
;;;   e^{-t} t^{a-1} (e^v - 1 - v), v = (x - a) log t, and `cc-exp-near-one' bounds it by
;;;   C (q - p) |x - a|^2, which `cc-diff-on-local-quadratic' (cc-diff-on-quadratic's local
;;;   form) turns into IS-DIFF-ON.  No exchange of limit and integral, no Fubini.
;;; * (5): on the ball of radius re(z0)/2 about z0, s0 = re(z0)/2 <= re z <= 3 re(z0)/2 = s1,
;;;   and `gamma-truncation-error' bounds |Gamma(z) - g_k(z)| by r_k^{s0}/s0 + 2 e^{K - R_k/2}
;;;   uniformly; `holomorphic-uniform-limit' (week 2) concludes.
;;; * (6): the tree has no integration by parts for CC-INT.  The notes' integration by parts is
;;;   the fundamental theorem for the product H(w) = -w^z e^{-w}, whose derivative is
;;;   GI(z + 1)(w) - z GI(z)(w) (`gamma-product-derivative'), with linearity; the boundary terms
;;;   |H(r)|, |H(R)| are the integrand at z + 1 and vanish by the bounds of (7).
;;;
;;; STATEMENT CHECKS.  The domain hypothesis is 0 < re z (`gamma-converges', `gamma-recursion');
;;; the holomorphy statement is HOLOMORPHIC-ON(H, w |-> GAMMA-FUNCTION(w)), the form of week 2.
